0 Four-Bar Linkage
0 Name: four-bar.ldr
0 Author: erik-larsen
0 // Four beams pinned in a loop: the frame (a 1x8 Technic brick, its end holes 6 studs
0 // apart), a 3L crank that turns all the way round, a 7L coupler, and a 5L rocker that
0 // rocks to and fro. Link lengths 2, 6 and 4 studs on a 6 stud base: the shortest link plus
0 // the longest (2 + 6) is less than the other two (6 + 4), so the shortest, next to the
0 // base, turns all the way round. Shown with the crank pointing straight up. The crank and
0 // rocker are in the layer in front of the brick, the coupler in the layer in front of them.

0 // Step 1: the frame, with pins in its end holes
1 14 0 0 0 -1 0 0 0 1 0 0 0 -1 3702.dat
1 0 60 10 -10 0 0 -1 0 1 0 1 0 0 3673.dat
1 0 -60 10 -10 0 0 -1 0 1 0 1 0 0 3673.dat
0 STEP

0 // Step 2: the crank and the rocker on those pins, each with a pin at its far end
1 4 60 -10 -20 -1 0 0 0 0 -1 0 -1 0 32523.dat
1 1 -56.61895 -29.85685 -20 -0.996421 0 0.084526 -0.084526 0 -0.996421 0 -1 0 32316.dat
1 0 60 -30 -30 0 0 -1 0 1 0 1 0 0 3673.dat
1 0 -53.2379 -69.7137 -30 0 0 -1 0 1 0 1 0 0 3673.dat
0 STEP

0 // Step 3: the coupler, across the two far ends
